<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>{{displayName}} — CallLint Support</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="CallLint support for {{displayName}} ({{vendor}}). {{#if coverageBoundary}}{{coverageBoundary}}{{else}}Full MCP configuration discovery and scanning.{{/if}}"
    />
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{canonicalUrl}}" />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.png" type="image/png" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="/logo-mark-256.png" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <a class="brand-lockup" href="/" aria-label="CallLint home">
        <img class="brand-mark" src="/logo-mark-128.png" width="40" height="40" alt="" />
        <span class="brand-name">CallLint</span>
      </a>
      <nav class="nav-links" aria-label="Primary">
        <a href="/">Home</a>
        <a href="/harnesses/">Harnesses</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/calllint/calllint">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/calllint">npm</a>
      </nav>
    </header>

    <main class="doc-content">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <a href="/">CallLint</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <a href="/harnesses/">Harnesses</a>
        <span aria-hidden="true">›</span>
        <span>{{displayName}}</span>
      </nav>

      <article>
        <header class="doc-header">
          <h1>{{displayName}}</h1>
          <p class="doc-lede">
            CallLint support for <strong>{{displayName}}</strong> by {{vendor}}.
            {{#if coverageBoundary}}
            <span class="coverage-note">{{coverageBoundary}}</span>
            {{/if}}
          </p>
          <div class="host-meta">
            <span class="badge badge-{{priority}}">{{priority}}</span>
            {{!-- The CSS hook keeps the internal class so stylesheets need no change; the
                  VISIBLE text is the public label. A human should learn what CallLint does
                  for this host, not which enum the codebase files it under. --}}
            <span class="badge badge-{{supportClass}}" title="{{supportLabelHint}}">{{supportLabel}}</span>
          </div>
        </header>

        {{!-- The activation contract (new20 Sprint 2). These three sections answer "why here?",
              "how do I start?" and "how do I verify?" — the questions a page that stated only a
              support level left a visitor holding. Order is deliberate: the reason to care comes
              before the instruction, and the instruction before the proof.

              EVERY STRING HERE IS DERIVED. `whyHere` and `firstSuccessAction` come from the
              SSOT's `activation` block; `installCommand` is resolved from project-facts.json
              through `activation.installRef`; `verifyCommand` is read off `truthfulCommands`,
              the field HD-01..HD-04 and HD-06 already audit. No command text is written in this
              template, and none is carried as prose in the SSOT — a command string in either
              place would be a second, unaudited advertiser of what CallLint can do. --}}
        <section id="why" class="doc-section">
          <h2>Why scan {{displayName}}?</h2>
          <p>{{activation.whyHere}}</p>
        </section>

        <section id="usage" class="doc-section">
          <h2>Usage</h2>
          {{#if truthfulCommands}}
          <p>CallLint can auto-discover and scan {{displayName}} configurations:</p>
          {{#each truthfulCommands}}
          <pre><code>{{this}}</code></pre>
          {{/each}}
          {{else}}
          <p>
            CallLint does not yet support native auto-discovery for {{displayName}}.
            {{#if supportLabelHint}}
            {{supportLabelHint}}
            {{/if}}
          </p>
          {{/if}}
        </section>

        {{!-- Guarded on `installCommand`, which the SSOT schema permits only for NATIVE and
              CONFIG_SCAN hosts. A guide-only page therefore prints no start path at all rather
              than a plausible one — the honest counterpart to its "Guide only" label. --}}
        {{#if activation.installCommand}}
        <section id="start" class="doc-section">
          <h2>How to start</h2>
          <p>Install nothing globally — run CallLint straight from npm:</p>
          <pre><code>{{activation.installCommand}}</code></pre>
          {{#if activation.verifyCommand}}
          <p>Then scan {{displayName}} specifically:</p>
          <pre><code>{{activation.verifyCommand}}</code></pre>
          {{/if}}
        </section>

        <section id="verify" class="doc-section">
          <h2>How to verify it worked</h2>
          <p>{{activation.firstSuccessAction}}</p>
          <p>
            A <strong>No blockers observed</strong> verdict means exactly that — no blocker under
            the evidence CallLint could collect. It is not a guarantee, and
            <strong>Insufficient evidence</strong> never becomes it on its own. See
            <a href="#coverage">Coverage Boundary</a> for what this scan does not look at.
          </p>
        </section>
        {{/if}}

        <section id="config" class="doc-section">
          <h2>Configuration Paths</h2>
          {{#if configEvidence}}
          <p>CallLint looks for {{displayName}} configurations in:</p>
          <ul>
            {{#each configEvidence}}
            <li><code>{{this}}</code></li>
            {{/each}}
          </ul>
          {{else}}
          <p>Configuration discovery requires verification.</p>
          {{/if}}
        </section>

        <section id="authority" class="doc-section">
          <h2>Authority Surfaces</h2>
          <p>{{displayName}} can grant tools the following authority surfaces:</p>
          <ul class="authority-list">
            {{#each authoritySurfaces}}
            <li><code>{{this}}</code></li>
            {{/each}}
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="distribution" class="doc-section">
          <h2>Distribution</h2>
          <p>CallLint is available for {{displayName}} through:</p>
          <ul class="distribution-list">
            {{#each distributionPrimitives}}
            <li>
              <strong>{{kind}}</strong>
              {{#if upstream}}
              <span class="upstream-note">(via <a href="https://registry.modelcontextprotocol.io/?q=calllint">{{upstream}}</a>)</span>
              {{/if}}
              {{!-- Public label + styling slug, both derived by `publicState()` in the
                    generator. Never `{{state}}`: that enum is an internal pipeline
                    primitive, and printing it made a visitor read "AUDIT_REQUIRED" with no
                    way to tell what it was a warning about. --}}
              — <span class="state-{{stateClass}}">{{stateLabel}}</span>
              {{#if note}}
              <div class="dist-note">{{note}}</div>
              {{/if}}
              {{#if blocker}}
              <div class="dist-blocker">⚠️ {{blocker}}</div>
              {{/if}}
            </li>
            {{/each}}
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="status" class="doc-section">
          <h2>Support Status</h2>
          {{!-- §16 question 5. The badge above states the label; this section states what
                the label MEANS for a reader's next action, which is the part a badge cannot
                carry. VISIBLE text is the public label and its hint only — never
                supportClass. §20 is enforced by check:agent-surface over this page's
                rendered text, so a token pasted here reds the build. --}}
          <p>
            <strong>{{supportLabel}}</strong>{{#if supportLabelHint}} — {{supportLabelHint}}{{/if}}
          </p>
          {{#if truthfulCommands}}
          <p>
            The commands under <a href="#usage">Usage</a> are the ones CallLint actually
            supports for {{displayName}} today. Anything not listed there is not claimed.
          </p>
          {{else}}
          <p>
            CallLint publishes no scan command for {{displayName}} yet. That is a statement
            about CallLint's coverage, not about {{displayName}}: see
            <a href="#coverage">Coverage Boundary</a> for what would have to be built first.
          </p>
          {{/if}}
        </section>

        <section id="sources" class="doc-section">
          <h2>Official Sources</h2>
          <ul>
            {{#each officialSources}}
            <li><a href="{{this}}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">{{this}}</a></li>
            {{/each}}
          </ul>
        </section>

        {{#if coverageBoundary}}
        <section id="coverage" class="doc-section coverage-boundary">
          <h2>Coverage Boundary</h2>
          <p class="boundary-text">{{coverageBoundary}}</p>
        </section>
        {{/if}}
      </article>

      <footer class="doc-footer">
        <p>
          Generated from <a href="https://github.com/calllint/calllint/blob/main/apps/web/data/distribution-surfaces.json">distribution-surfaces.json</a>
          — canonical source of truth for CallLint's global agent distribution authority.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/harnesses/">← Back to Harnesses</a> |
          <a href="/">CallLint Home</a>
        </p>
      </footer>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>

